        "content": [
          "For TS recruitment,",
          "the first step is to advise unsuccessful candidates.",
          "check if the candidate has accepted a voluntary redundancy.",
          "If the candidate has not accepted, the process continues.",
          "The recruitment manager sends an Appointment Approval form, which is then received by the next level manager.",
          "If the manager is an external resource, they may not authorize the form. However, if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues.",
          "if the approver is an existing employee of the client, the process continues. If the form is approved, the recruitment manager sends the form and other documentation",
          "which is received by the client HR. The HR department scans the completed form and records the position against the stored position in GovSource.",
          "Otherwise, the process continues. The Appointment Approval is carried forward.",
          "If the position requires a medical assessment, it is applicable for a 12% rate.",
          "For the step of the Preferred Candidate's medical assessments, it is important to note that it can take up to 21 days to arrange and complete.",
          "The TS HR coordinator informs the recruitment manager, who then liaises with the HR representative to confirm the offer to the candidate.",
          "If the assessment is not satisfactory, the next candidate on the shortlist should be contacted."
        ]
      },
